I’m screening a structural idea locally: replace later preactivation marginals by rank-preserving Gaussian quantiles with the same estimated moments. That can reduce marginal Monte Carlo noise, but it may also erase useful correlation with the official Monte Carlo target, so I’ll test it synthetically first.
